    "result_text": "All tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `salutation` feature for owners. The request may include a `title` (`MR`/`MRS`/`MS`/`DR`), and the owner's response now carries `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nSince this project generates its DTOs from `openapi.yml` and persists owners between the create (POST) and read-back (GET), the change spans four layers:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\n   - Added a `title` input property (enum `MR/MRS/MS/DR`) to the `OwnerFields` schema.\n   - Added a read-only `salutation` property to the `Owner` schema.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter so the title survives POST\u2192GET.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"salutation\", expression = \"java(salutation(owner))\")` plus a `salutation(Owner)` default method that composes `title + \" \" + lastName`, falling back to `lastName` when the title is null/blank. (`title` itself maps automatically by name, with MapStruct handling the enum\u2194String conversion.)\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table in all four `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` files (the test uses the `hsqldb` profile). Seed `data.sql` inserts use explicit column lists, so they were unaffected.\n\nNo OfficeFloor YAML changes were needed: the existing create pipeline (`ValidateOwnerFields` republishes the same body object, so `title` is preserved \u2192 `BuildOwner` \u2192 `SaveOwner`) and read pipeline (`LoadOwner` \u2192 `RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `toOwnerDto`) already carry the DTOs through the mapper.\n\n**Test results:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation`, asserting `$.salutation == \"DR who\"`, passes).",
